        <td>Quarterly</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 class="sub">9.3 Reserves &amp; account waterfall</h3>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><b>Debt Service Reserve Account (DSRA)</b> — funded to cover next 6 months of debt service at COD; topped up from operating cashflow until 12-month cover at year 5.</li>
    <li><b>Maintenance Reserve Account (MRA)</b> — funded annually at 1.0% of CapEx for 10 years (peak £{{ '%.1f'|format((lender_terms.debt_amount + lender_terms.equity_amount) * 0.10 / 1e6) }}m); released against approved capex programme.</li>
    <li><b>Major Maintenance Reserve (MMRA)</b> — funded from year 5 onwards for chiller/transformer overhaul cycles; sized to LTA-confirmed asset-replacement plan.</li>
    <li><b>Decommissioning sinking fund</b> — escrow at £4,000/MW/yr (Ofgem guidance) — peak £{{ '%.1f'|format(project.capacity_mw * 4000 * 20 / 1e6) }}m at year 20.</li>
    <li><b>Distribution lock-up</b> — distributions blocked when DSCR &lt; 1.20x or DSRA &lt; 6-month minimum.</li>
  </ul>
