{# Risk mitigation playbook                                                   #}
{# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section class="section">
  <h2 class="section-title">12.1 · Risk Mitigation Playbook</h2>

  <p class="section-intro">
    For each amber- and red-rated risk, the table below states the proposed
    mitigation actions, the responsible party and the trigger condition that
    escalates the risk.
  </p>

  <table class="data">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Risk</th>
        <th>Mitigation strategy</th>
        <th>Owner</th>
        <th>Escalation trigger</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Grid connection slippage</td>
        <td>Lock Bilateral Connection Agreement with date-certain LDs at FID; dual-feed candidate roster pre-cleared by SQSS (§3.3); engage NGET MSIP +6-mo accelerated delivery option (CCCM v19 §8).</td>
        <td>Grid Lead</td>
        <td>NESO offer slips beyond P50 by &gt; 3 months</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Anchor tenant pre-lease</td>
        <td>Pre-FID heads of terms with 2 named hyperscalers; sponsor parent guarantee for shortfall; develop fallback colocation strategy via UK iDC operators (Telehouse / VIRTUS / Ark).</td>
        <td>Commercial Director</td>
        <td>Pre-let drops below 40% by FID-3 months</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>EPC delivery slip (Tier-3 build)</td>
        <td>Date-certain EPC with capped LDs (15% of contract sum); performance bond 10%; retention 5%; direct-agreement with key sub-contractors; weekly Lender Technical Advisor (LTA) reporting from M3.</td>
        <td>EPC Counterparty</td>
        <td>Programme float falls below 4 weeks</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Switchgear &amp; transformer lead times</td>
        <td>Place orders on signed Pre-Order Direct Agreements at FID-1 month; Sponsor IDC carry on long-lead items; cross-shop AIS substitute if GIS slips beyond 22 months.</td>
        <td>Procurement</td>
        <td>OEM commitment slips beyond contract LD</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cyber &amp; operational resilience (DORA)</td>
        <td>SCADA / BMS air-gap segmentation per IEC 62443 SL-2; quarterly red-team simulation; tabletop exercises; 3rd-party SOC2 Type II monitoring; mandatory notification under NIS-2.</td>
        <td>CTO</td>
        <td>Material incident event or sustained anomaly</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cooling water-stress (immersion / evap path)</td>
        <td>Pre-application abstraction-licence engagement with EA; rainwater capture + grey-water-system; site-specific Drought Plan per Defra guidance; A2 dry-cooler fallback design retained.</td>
        <td>Environmental Lead</td>
        <td>EA refuses abstraction licence or imposes unworkable conditions</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Embodied carbon vs RICS PS 2023</td>
        <td>Specify CEMIII concrete + recycled steel (45% reduction); BREEAM Outstanding registration; 3rd-party WLCA audit at RIBA 4; offset balance via Article 6.4 ITMOs.</td>
        <td>Sustainability Lead</td>
        <td>Whole-life-carbon benchmark exceeded by &gt; 10%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Climate Change Agreement Vol 4 levy relief</td>
        <td>Maintain &lt; 1.20 PUE throughout reporting cycle; submit ESOS Phase-3 audit on time; engage Carbon Trust as approved verifier; build IT-load metering granular to rack level.</td>
        <td>ESG Lead</td>
        <td>Annual PUE drift past 1.25 sustained for &gt; 2 quarters</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Refinancing risk (Year 15 mini-perm)</td>
        <td>Lock refinance window 24 months pre-maturity; alternative public-debt take-out via DC-ABS market; equity holdco bridge facility at sponsor level.</td>
        <td>Treasury</td>
        <td>Credit market spreads widen beyond +75 bps vs base case</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Insurance market hardening</td>
        <td>Lock 3-yr LTA with primary placement at execution; quota-share with reinsurance (Munich Re / Hannover Re); periodic market-test at year 3 + 6 + 9.</td>
        <td>Insurance Broker</td>
        <td>Annual premium increase &gt; CPI + 2.5pp at renewal</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 class="sub">Critical-path interventions (top-3 lever)</h3>
  <ol style="margin-left: 6mm; font-size: 10pt; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.6;">
    <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5mm;"><b>Pre-FID dual-feed Construction Agreement.</b> Removing the Grid amber-flag is the single highest-leverage action; the BCA + acceleration option turns +6 to +9 months of P50 risk into a single, contractually-bounded delay.</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5mm;"><b>Anchor-tenant binding term sheet at FID.</b> An executed pre-lease with an investment-grade tenant unlocks the senior margin step-down, materially improving DSCR and base IRR.</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5mm;"><b>BREEAM Outstanding + ESRS aligned reporting from year 1.</b> Catalyses the SLB ratchet (-15 bps margin reduction at year 5 if ESRS PUE / WUE / CFE targets met) and unlocks EU Taxonomy-aligned investor base.</li>
  </ol>
</section>


